# Every setting Captcher reads. Your settings file is ~/.captcher/.env
# (CAPTCHER_HOME/.env), which `captcher` creates on first run with the common
# ones commented out; copy any line from here into it. Loaded by envfile.py.
#
# How it is read, because this has caused confusion before: only names ABSENT
# from the environment are filled in, and the file is read top-down. So a real
# shell variable beats this file entirely, and the FIRST occurrence of a
# duplicated key wins — a second ANTHROPIC_API_KEY further down is silently ignored.
# The file is read once at import; changes need a restart, and developer
# mode (`captcher --dev`) only watches .py files.
#
# There is no prefix-compatibility layer. Every knob below is read under the
# name written here and no other.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Required if the key above is NOT scoped to a workspace (the API answers 400
# "must include the anthropic-workspace-id header" without it). Find the ID in
# the Console under Settings > Workspaces; it starts with wrkspc_. A key that
# was created inside a workspace does not need this.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...

# Optional: Google Fonts Developer API key. With it, the Branding page's font
# picker offers the full ~1,800-family catalogue with live previews; without it
# it falls back to a curated ~50-font list. Free key at
# https://developers.google.com/fonts/docs/developer_api
# GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY=AIza...

# --- Where data lives (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Everything this server keeps: .env, session_secret, captcher.db (SQLite) and
# captures/ (every captured page and image). Default ~/.captcher. Back this
# folder up to back Captcher up.
# CAPTCHER_HOME has to be set in your shell, NOT in this file: it is what says
# where this file is.
#   export CAPTCHER_HOME=~/captcher-data
# Put the database somewhere other than CAPTCHER_HOME/captcher.db.
# CAPTCHER_DB=

# --- Access (only when listening beyond this machine) --------------------
# There are no accounts. Bound to 127.0.0.1 (the default), the browser on this
# machine is the owner and nothing is needed. To listen on other addresses
# (CAPTCHER_HOST=0.0.0.0), the server REQUIRES an access token: people
# enter it once at /unlock and get a cookie. Use a long random string.
# CAPTCHER_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#
# Extra host names a loopback-bound server answers to (comma-separated), for
# a local alias or proxy. Any other Host header is refused, which is what
# keeps web pages from reaching this server through DNS rebinding.
# CAPTCHER_ALLOWED_HOSTS=captcher.localhost
#
# Attempts per client per window at /unlock, and the window in seconds.
# CAPTCHER_UNLOCK_RATE_LIMIT=20
# CAPTCHER_UNLOCK_RATE_WINDOW=900
#
# Optional: pin the cookie-signing key so the access cookie survives moving
# machines. Unset, a random key is generated and kept in CAPTCHER_HOME/session_secret.
# CAPTCHER_SESSION_SECRET=choose-a-long-random-string
#
# Set only if this server sits behind a proxy that sets X-Forwarded-For and
# X-Forwarded-Proto. Without it both headers are ignored, because trusting a
# forgeable header would let one attacker present a fresh address per request.
# CAPTCHER_TRUST_PROXY=1
#
# Force the access cookie's Secure flag. Unset means "on only when a trusted
# proxy reports HTTPS". Set it when serving over HTTPS. Forcing it on while
# actually serving http locks everybody out: the browser accepts the cookie and
# never sends it back.
# CAPTCHER_SECURE_COOKIES=1

# --- Tests and examples (optional) --------------------------------------
# Optional explicit recorder checkout, read only by the cross-component
# contract tests. Otherwise the repository's own extension/ folder is used.
# CAPTCHER_EXTENSION_DIR=/path/to/extension
#
# Comma-separated walkthrough slugs shown as full-page public examples at
# /examples/<slug> (maximum five). Listing one is not enough to publish it:
# each must also have "Enable embedding" switched on. Configuration alone never
# makes a private walkthrough public.
# CAPTCHER_EXAMPLE_WALKTHROUGHS=work-a-ticket,log-a-new-ticket

# --- Authoring (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Override the model for every Claude call — authoring, AI edit, render and
# replay checks, brand inference (default claude-sonnet-5-5).
# CAPTCHER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# Thinking depth for the Stage 3 authoring pass (default high). Sonnet 5.5
# accepts low, medium, high, xhigh and max.
# CAPTCHER_AUTHOR_EFFORT=high
# Thinking depth for the AI edit pass and verify's repair turn (default medium).
# CAPTCHER_EDIT_EFFORT=medium

# --- Observability (optional) --------------------------------------------
# LangSmith tracing for the three Claude calls (authoring pass, AI edit, brand
# inference). Off unless BOTH of the first two are set.
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_pt_...
# LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=Captcher
# Per-string cap on what a trace carries. Prompts here are captured customer
# pages — an authoring pass can hold close to a million tokens of third-party
# HTML — so every traced string is clipped to this many characters. 0 sends the
# lot; raise it knowing what leaves the machine.
# CAPTCHER_LANGSMITH_MAX_CHARS=20000

# Talking to extensions that are already installed. Both unset by default, and
# both are read by the extension on every connect check, so a change takes
# effect without anyone reinstalling anything.
#
# A free-text line the recorder shows in a banner above every screen. For the
# things a version number cannot say. Under 300 characters; the panel truncates.
# CAPTCHER_EXTENSION_NOTICE=Uploads are paused until 14:00 UTC. Nothing you have recorded is lost.
#
# The oldest extension version this server still works with. A recorder below
# it stops offering to pair and tells the user to load the newer recorder,
# rather than failing somewhere less obvious.
# CAPTCHER_MIN_EXTENSION=1.0.0

# Note: the capture extension does not use a shared env token. Each browser
# gets its own capture token by pairing (open the recorder's side panel on a
# Captcher page). For scripts, `captcher token` mints one.

# --- Developer mode ---------------------------------------------------------
# Restart on code changes, re-read templates, show tracebacks. Same as
# `captcher --dev`. Off by default.
# CAPTCHER_DEBUG=1
